  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nFirefox has non-standard `scrollLeftMax` and `scrollTopMax` props which we need in all browsers. Currently there's literally no way to reliably tell if a container is scrolled all the way to the end.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nUsing basic math like `scrollWidth - scrollLeft - clientWidth` is broken due to subpixels, especially in zooms outside 100%.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nExpose `scrollLeftMax` and `scrollTopMax` like Firefox does so people can just use `scrollLeft === scrollLeftMax`\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
